[{"_1":2,"_3":4},"root",{"_5":113},"en/routes/conteudo-do-cubo.tsx",{"_5":6},"data",{"_7":8,"_9":10,"_11":12,"_13":14,"_15":16,"_17":18,"_19":20,"_21":22,"_23":24,"_25":26},"tipo","metodo","cubo",{"_11":111,"_13":111,"_29":112},"id","reducao","nome","Reduction","nomeLongo","Centers, edges and like a 3x3","termo",{"_29":108,"_109":110},"niveis",[57],"introducao","<p>As on the 4x4: build the centers, <a href=\"/en/glossary#par\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"A corner and an edge that go together into the same slot in F2L.\">pair</a> the edges and solve it like a 3x3. On the 5x5 the centers have 9 pieces and the edges 3; on the other hand, there is no <a href=\"/en/glossary#paridade\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"On the 4x4 (and even cubes), situations that don't exist on the 3x3: a single flipped edge (OLL Parity) or two swapped pieces (PLL Parity).…\">parity</a> in the 3x3 part. Open each step with the cube in your hand.</p>\n","etapas",[33,34,35],"historias",[27],{"_13":28,"_29":30,"_31":32},"The 5x5 and reduction","endereco","/historia#5x5","resumo","The 5x5 (Professor's Cube) was created by Udo Krell in 1981 and made by Uwe Mèffert from 1983.",{"_11":78,"_13":79,"_38":80,"_40":81,"_42":82,"_43":83,"_44":84},{"_11":46,"_13":47,"_38":48,"_40":49,"_42":50,"_43":51,"_44":52},{"_11":36,"_13":37,"_38":39,"_40":41,"_42":-7,"_43":-7,"_44":45},"3x3","Like a 3x3","html","<p>With centers and edges done, solve it like a 3x3, turning only the outer faces (<code>R</code>, <code>U</code>, <code>F</code>…): the <a href=\"/en/3x3/beginner\">3x3 beginner method</a> or <a href=\"/en/glossary#cfop\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"The most used method in competitions: the cross, the 4 F2L pairs, OLL (makes the top face one color) and PLL (puts the top pieces in place).\">CFOP</a> work just the same. Don&#39;t turn the inner layers: they break up the centers and the edges.</p>\n","grupos",[],"pagina","treino","imagem","/imagens/diagramas/1d85b938ad2a2bb4.svg","arestas","Edges","<p>Join the 3 pieces of each edge; the last 2 have cases (<a href=\"/en/glossary#l2e\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"In the 5x5 reduction: joins the pieces of the last 2 edges, finishing the reduction.\">L2E</a>). Then, solve it like a 3x3: on the 5x5 there is no <a href=\"/en/glossary#paridade\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"On the 4x4 (and even cubes), situations that don't exist on the 3x3: a single flipped edge (OLL Parity) or two swapped pieces (PLL Parity).…\">parity</a> in that part.</p>\n",[54],{"_13":47,"_29":53},"/5x5/treino?grupo=l2e","/imagens/diagramas/8b8d9b65967bf45c.svg","/5x5/arestas",{"_11":55,"_13":55,"_56":57,"_58":59,"_60":61,"_62":63,"_29":64},"L2E","nivel","intermediario","casos",13,"conjunto",false,"ids",[65,66,67,68,69,70,71,72,73,74,75,76,77],"/5x5/l2e","5X5-L2E1","5X5-L2E2","5X5-L2E3","5X5-L2E4","5X5-L2E5","5X5-L2E6","5X5-L2E7","5X5-L2E8","5X5-L2E9","5X5-L2E10","5X5-L2E11","5X5-L2E12","5X5-L2E13","centros","Centers","<p>Build the centers (9 pieces each). The first four are intuitive; the last 2 have cases (<a href=\"/en/glossary#l2c\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"In the 5x5 reduction: builds the last 2 centers (the top and front ones).\">L2C</a>).</p>\n",[86],{"_13":79,"_29":85},"/5x5/treino?grupo=l2c","/imagens/diagramas/408218b0821c7268.svg","/5x5/centros",{"_11":87,"_13":87,"_56":57,"_58":88,"_60":61,"_62":89,"_29":90},"L2C",17,[91,92,93,94,95,96,97,98,99,100,101,102,103,104,105,106,107],"/5x5/l2c","5X5-L2C1","5X5-L2C2","5X5-L2C3","5X5-L2C4","5X5-L2C5","5X5-L2C6","5X5-L2C7","5X5-L2C8","5X5-L2C9","5X5-L2C10","5X5-L2C11","5X5-L2C12","5X5-L2C13","5X5-L2C14","5X5-L2C15","5X5-L2C16","5X5-L2C17","/en/glossary#reducao","dica","For 4x4 and 5x5: build the centers and pair up the edges until the cube is like a 3x3, which is solved the usual way.","5x5","/5x5/",{"_114":115,"_116":117},"cubos",[120,121,122,123,124,125,126],"idiomas",[118,119],"pt","en",{"_11":36,"_13":36},{"_11":134,"_13":134},{"_11":133,"_13":133},{"_11":111,"_13":111},{"_11":131,"_13":132},{"_11":129,"_13":130},{"_11":127,"_13":128},"skewb","Skewb","pyraminx","Pyraminx","megaminx","Megaminx","4x4","2x2"]
